      "playwright": "Most assertions target data-* state (data-pass, data-status) rather than colours, which keeps the report tests exact. The catastrophic-backtracking case uses real time on purpose: the 750 ms watchdog is a real setTimeout racing a real Worker, so page.clock is not installed and the assertion simply allows up to 5 s for the warning. Debounced inputs are handled by Playwright's auto-retrying expects rather than fixed sleeps. localStorage is cleared in beforeEach so the persistence test starts from zero, and the win is then verified across page.reload(). No screenshots — every behaviour has a text or attribute oracle.",
      "coverage": [
        "Pass/fail report counts and failure reasons",
        "Capture group highlighting and listing",
        "Plain-English explanation, flag sensitivity and cheat-sheet insertion",
        "Friendly compile errors with cases left unrun",
        "Catastrophic backtracking timeout and recovery",
        "Challenge round win and persistence"
      ]
