      "playwright": "The editor reads cells from pointer events, so the spec works out each cell's centre from the canvas bounding box and the grid size, then uses locator.click with a position, or page.mouse down/move/up for line drags. This works the same on the Pixel 7 profile because Playwright's mouse sends pointer events. Downloads were easy to test with waitForEvent('download'), and reading the PNG header from the saved file checks the real output size without an image library. Feeding that same file to setInputFiles made a real round trip. The one timing-dependent feature, the preview player, runs on setInterval under a paused fake clock. toHaveScreenshot was avoided in favour of the pixel hook.",
